@startuml users
title Users: application use cases and domain persistence
autonumber
actor "User" as User
participant "CLI / TUI\nPresentation" as Client
participant "CLI internal/app" as ClientApp
participant "Document client\nHTTP OR gRPC adapter" as Remote
box "hermes-document-service" #E0F4E0
participant "API + session middleware" as API
participant "internal/app" as App
participant "internal/domain\nPolicies / invariants" as Domain
participant "internal/postgres\nUnitOfWork / repositories" as Repo
end box
database "Document PostgreSQL" as DB
note over Remote, App
  Protected requests follow auth.puml: middleware -> Auth -> Redis SessionStore.
  Only a valid session reaches the use case; Redis failure returns unavailable.
  App receives authenticated identity, never a client-supplied actor ID.
  Domain access checks use current data through repositories.
end note
note over App, DB
  Mutations use one PostgreSQL transaction with current access and version checks.
  Any failed check rolls back all writes; unchanged state creates no change event.
  Domain facts from committed changes follow events_dispatch.puml.
  Outbox/CDC versus direct publication remains OPEN (ADR-002).
end note

== Register ==
User -> Client : Register(username, display_name, email, credentials)
Client -> ClientApp : Users.Register
ClientApp -> Remote : Register(request)
Remote -> API : Public request over TLS; no session required
API -> App : Users.Register(validated DTO)
App -> App : CredentialVerifier prepares verifier data\nvia internal/credentials (method OPEN)
App -> Repo : WithinTransaction
Repo -> DB : BEGIN
App -> Domain : Validate identity and personal workspace invariants
App -> Repo : Create user + credentials + personal workspace + owner membership
Repo -> DB : INSERT; enforce normalized identity uniqueness
alt Invalid input, uniqueness conflict or persistence failure
  Repo -> DB : ROLLBACK
  App --> API : Validation / conflict / unavailable
else All writes valid
  Repo -> DB : COMMIT
  App --> API : Profile + personal workspace; facts ready for publication
end
API --> Remote : Map result to transport DTO / error
Remote --> ClientApp : Application result
ClientApp --> Client : Profile or error
Client --> User : Show result; login is a separate operation
note over App, DB
  UserCreated, WorkspaceCreated, WorkspaceMemberAdded describe committed changes.
  These facts do not create personal notifications by themselves.
  Lost registration response: outcome unknown; retry/recovery contract is OPEN.
end note

== Read private or public profile ==
User -> Client : Open own / another user's profile
Client -> ClientApp : Users.GetSelf / GetPublicProfile
ClientApp -> Remote : Profile query
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Users.GetSelf(actor) / GetPublicProfile(actor, target)
App -> Repo : Read active profile with required visibility predicate
Repo -> DB : SELECT; public profile requires shared active workspace membership
DB --> Repo : Allowed fields or unavailable
Repo --> App : Profile
App --> API : Own email only in private profile; no credentials
API --> Remote : DTO / error
Remote --> ClientApp : Profile / error
ClientApp --> Client : Result

== Update username / display name ==
ClientApp -> Remote : UpdateSelf(changes, expected_version)
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Users.UpdateSelf(actor, changes, expected_version)
App -> Repo : WithinTransaction; load active user and version
Repo -> DB : BEGIN; read/lock current row
App -> Domain : Validate fields, expected_version and actual changes
alt Valid changed values
  App -> Repo : Update user and increment version
  Repo -> DB : UPDATE with identity constraints; COMMIT if valid
  App --> API : Updated profile; UserUpdated fact after commit
else Unchanged or rejected
  Repo -> DB : COMMIT without writes / ROLLBACK on error
  App --> API : Current profile / conflict / validation error
end
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result
note over App
  ProfileChanged policy: notify owner for username/email changes, if enabled.
  Display-name-only changes have no personal notification.
end note

== Change email ==
ClientApp -> Remote : RequestEmailChange(new_email, expected_version)
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Users.RequestEmailChange(actor, request)
App -> Repo : Transaction: check active user/version; store expiring token hash
Repo -> DB : Persist pending request; current email unchanged
App --> API : Confirmation required
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Confirmation required
note over App, DB
  Confirmation delivery and initial email verification remain OPEN.
  Confirmation secrets never enter domain events or notification inbox.
end note
User -> Client : Confirm new email using one-time token
Client -> ClientApp : Users.ConfirmEmail
ClientApp -> Remote : ConfirmEmail(token)
Remote -> API : Confirmation request over TLS
API -> App : Users.ConfirmEmail(token)
App -> Repo : Transaction: check token, expiry, active user and uniqueness;\nchange only email, increment version, consume token
Repo -> DB : Commit all changes or roll back
App --> API : Updated profile + UserUpdated fact after commit / error
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result

== Delete account ==
ClientApp -> Remote : GetDeletionBlockers
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Users.GetDeletionBlockers(actor)
App -> Repo : Find active shared workspaces owned by actor
Repo -> DB : SELECT ownership blockers
Repo --> App : Blockers
App --> API : Blockers; preliminary check only
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Blockers
ClientApp --> Client : Require transfer/deletion first, or ask identity confirmation
User -> Client : Confirm account deletion
Client -> ClientApp : Users.DeleteSelf(confirmation, expected_version)
ClientApp -> Remote : DeleteSelf
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Users.DeleteSelf(actor, confirmation, expected_version)
App -> App : Verify identity through CredentialVerifier
ref over App, DB
  OPEN coordination protocol (ADR-001): domain deletion in PostgreSQL
  and revocation of all user sessions in Redis; no shared transaction
end ref
note over App, DB
  Domain transaction rechecks active user/version and ownership blockers.
  Serialize against ownership transfer, new memberships and invitations.
  Mark user deleted; close personal workspace/documents; remove memberships,
  subscriptions and pending confirmations; revoke affected invitations.
  Retain shared-document attribution as "Deleted user".
  Facts: UserDeleted, WorkspaceDeleted, membership/invitation changes.
  No success until domain deletion AND session revocation are confirmed.
  Ordering, retries and reconciliation must be agreed before implementation.
end note
App --> API : Confirmed deletion / conflict / unavailable / outcome unknown
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result
ClientApp -> ClientApp : Clear local session only on confirmed deletion\nor explicit unauthenticated response
ClientApp --> Client : Result; keep unknown outcome visible
@enduml
